    "body": "## P1 authorization/privacy hardening\n\nSaved-job endpoints expose user-specific bookmark state. The service previously dereferenced `user.getId()` throughout individual status, batch status, remove and list flows, while save loaded a job before proving the authenticated principal had a persisted identity. Security middleware should normally provide a principal, but service-layer authorization boundaries must fail closed independently and must not touch persistence for a missing/transient identity.\n\n### Change\n- add one `requireUserId` identity gate shared by every SavedJob operation;\n- validate identity before loading a target job or querying bookmark state;\n- reuse the validated immutable user id for ownership/bookmark repository predicates;\n- preserve public job visibility and block-list semantics for authenticated users;\n- return the existing authorization exception family rather than allowing null dereferences/internal errors.\n\n### Regression coverage\n- null principal and principal without persisted id are rejected across save/remove/status/batch/list;\n- regression proves no SavedJob, Job, JobService or block-service repository/domain access occurs before identity validation;\n- existing open-job privacy scoping, own-job rejection, block handling, idempotency, batch deduplication and list cleanup tests remain intact.\n\nRebased/reconstructed cleanly on current `master` `4b85fb8402d27f0db598e2ce29a6be6d6c079c30`; the two touched files were unchanged on master since the original base.\n\nMerge policy: exact current head only; all relevant checks green; no unresolved review threads; revalidate master immediately before merge; merge commit only.",
